   "tests": [
    {
     "id": "eqweather_scm_traj_step1410_60s",
     "description": "ONE WRF STEP INTEGRATED: the step-1410 column of couplings/eqweather_scm.esm (initial state = wrfout frame 1409 of the em_scm_xy reference run, 18:29 UTC, bitwise the same initial_conditions and parameter_overrides as that document's step-1410 test) advanced by diffsol BDF from t = 0 to 60 s at the runner's default solver tolerance, and compared at t = 60 s with WRF. REFERENCES, all from real32 WRF (../WRF/main/wrf.exe): (1) data/eqwefic/scm_ref_perstep, the reference namelist rerun with 1-min history, bitwise equal to data/eqwefic/scm_ref at every hourly frame; t = 60 s is frame 1410. (2) data/eqwefic/scm_ref_dtsens, restarts from the 18:29 state at dt = 60/30/15/6 s (dt = 60 reproduces (1) bitwise). WRF's dt -> 0 limit is estimated by the first-order extrapolation (15 X6 - 6 X15)/9; its uncertainty, taken as the spread between that and (30 X15 - 15 X30)/15, is u 1.8e-4 m/s, v 3.6e-5 m/s, theta_m 4.2e-4 K, q_v 1.7e-8 kg/kg. Numbers transcribed by tools/fill_eqweather_scm_trajectory.py. WHY THE dt -> 0 LIMIT: the document is a continuous ODE, so its trajectory converges to WRF's as WRF's step shrinks, not to WRF at dt = 60 s. WRF's own splitting error after one step (|X(dt=6) - X(dt=60)|, Linf over the column) is u 2.8e-3, v 9.8e-4, theta_m 3.4e-3 K, q_v 4.5e-7, w 6.1e-5 (1.0e-4 at dt = 30), phi' 1.6e-2, TSK and TSLB 5.8e-4, against a one-step signal of u 1.6e-2, v 1.4e-2, theta_m 1.7e-2, q_v 2.0e-5, phi' 0.43, TSK 8.2e-3. MEASURED (Linf, ESM minus reference at t = 60 s; against WRF dt = 60 / dt = 6 / dt -> 0): u 3.0e-3 / 2.4e-4 / 1.7e-4; v 1.1e-3 / 2.6e-4 / 2.2e-4; theta_m 4.1e-3 / 7.1e-4 / 3.2e-4; q_v 5.1e-7 / 6.6e-8 / 2.4e-8; w 7.5e-5 / 1.0e-4 / 1.2e-4; phi' 8.7e-3 / 8.9e-3 / 1.5e-2; T_s and T_sk 4.0e-4 / 9.8e-4 / 1.2e-3; q_i 6.8e-13 / 3.4e-12 / 4.3e-12. So u, v, theta_m and q_v are 10-20x closer to WRF's dt -> 0 limit than to WRF's own dt = 60 answer, and within ~1-2x the extrapolation's own uncertainty: they are asserted against the dt -> 0 limit at 2-3x the measured residual (u 4e-4, v 5e-4, theta_m 1e-3, q_v 5e-8), every one of them several times TIGHTER than WRF's splitting error, so the test would fail against the dt = 60 answer and pins the continuous limit. w, phi', q_i, T_s and T_sk do not converge that way and are asserted against WRF at its own dt = 60 s, at about 1.5x the WRF dt spread: w and phi' carry the undamped vertical acoustic mode (this document has no acoustic sub-step or off-centring, so it is a different mode amplitude, not a convergence), w abs 1.5e-4 and phi' abs 2e-2; q_i is trace cirrus (<= 2.1e-9) at abs 5e-12; T_s and T_sk at abs 8e-4 K sit closer to WRF dt = 60 than to its dt -> 0 limit (4.0e-4 against 1.2e-3), which is NOT understood and is listed as open in the notes (a candidate is that the WRF slab and surface layer read a lagged skin temperature whose effect scales with dt, which a continuous coupling cannot reproduce). q_c is asserted to stay at zero to 1e-20 (WRF has no cloud water anywhere). Prescribed for the whole minute, as in the t = 0 test: cos zenith, psfc and the surface layer's previous-step fields (ust_prev, mol_prev, ...). Over 60 s cos zenith moves ~1e-3 relative; not separated from the residuals above. MEASURED 10/10 on ./esm 00808ba51 (ESD_ROOT main-431bd46), 2026-11-20, load 10-14 on 20 cores: 860 s wall, 990 s CPU, peak 408 MB, almost all of it the finite-difference Jacobian (2 x 656 + 1 right-hand-side evaluations) and its refreshes; a run at --reltol 1e-6 was not faster.",
     "parameter_overrides": {
